    "tarball_url":  "https://api.github.com/repos/topjohnwu/samloader-rs/tarball/2.2.0",
    "zipball_url":  "https://api.github.com/repos/topjohnwu/samloader-rs/zipball/2.2.0",
    "body":  "### Features\r\n\r\n- **Resumable Downloads**: Firmware downloads now save to `.part` files with embedded metadata and bitfield tracking, allowing seamless resumption; added `-f`/`--force` to restart from scratch (#29).\r\n- **Automatic PIT Flashing**: Removed `--repartition`; PIT files are now automatically committed whenever available (from archives or `--pit`), matching Odin4 behavior.\r\n- **Dynamic Partition Validation**: Implemented pre-flight capacity checks (opcode `0x6a`) and automatic `super_used_size` detection from raw, sparse, and LZ4 `super.img` metadata. This allows flashing super partition without repartitioning.\r\n- **Device Diagnostics**: Added hardware specification inspection in `samloader detect` using pre-handshake `DVIF` and opcode `0x69` TLV dumps (with `--json` output).\r\n- **Extended Flash Controls**:\r\n  - `--csc-code \u003cCODE\u003e`: Configure persistent device sales code via opcode `0x64`.\r\n  - `-e, --erase`: Perform low-level `USERDATA` NAND block wiping via opcode `0x64`.\r\n  - `--redownload`: Reboot directly back into Download Mode via opcode `0x67`.\r\n- **Legacy `.enc2` Support**: Added download and MD5-derived AES decryption for older Samsung firmware packages.\r\n\r\n### Bug Fixes \u0026 Reliability\r\n\r\n- **USB Connection Stability**: Replaced disruptive USB bus resets with `clear_halt` and a non-blocking IN buffer drain, resolving `FAILunknown command` errors on Snapdragon UEFI and timeouts on newer tablets (#27, #37).\r\n- **Odin4 Protocol Alignment**:\r\n  - Matched official Zero-Length Packet (ZLP) rules: eliminated ZLPs during chunk streaming and limited control ZLPs to legacy devices (`\"Gadget Serial\"`).\r\n  - Fixed slice transfer state by sending init packets before every sequence and rounding raw slice announcements to 128 KB boundaries.\r\n  - Added uncompressed size reporting for LZ4 transfer announcements.\r\n- **Error Handling**: Introduced `LokeError` to map bootloader negative status codes and prevent silent failures.\r\n- **Manifest Validation**: Correctly propagate corrupted archive and manifest errors (`download-list.txt`, `super_used_size.txt`) instead of ignoring them (#39).\r\n- **Download Metrics**: Fixed EMA speed and ETA calculation spikes when resuming partial downloads.\r\n\r\n### Architecture \u0026 Performance\r\n\r\n- **Session \u0026 Flashing Pipeline**: Split connection lifecycle into `OdinConnection` (handshake) and `OdinSession` (protocol), orchestrated via a fluent `FlashManager` builder.\r\n- **Zero-Copy \u0026 Memory Optimizations**: Lazily memory-map only partitions selected for flashing and eliminate heap allocations in packet serialization using stack buffers and `Cow\u003c[u8]\u003e`.\r\n- **Global Progress Reporter**: Streamlined CLI callbacks through a process-wide `FlashProgress` reporter and added real-time MD5 verification progress.\r\n- **Portability \u0026 Mocks**: Fixed Linux compilation (`libc`), expanded mock USB device profiles (SM-F968B, GT-I9305), aligned protocol terminology with Odin4/LOKE, and pruned unused dependencies and derives.\r\n\r\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/topjohnwu/samloader-rs/compare/2.1.0...2.2.0",
